# Anchored. `go build ./cmd/perfcompare` from this directory drops the binary
# at test/performance/perfcompare, which is what these patterns are for. Written
# bare, they also matched the cmd/perfcompare/ DIRECTORY, so that package's
# main.go was invisible to `git add .` and was never committed.
/perfcompare
/perfcompare.remote

# Log of a detached remote run (see run-remote.sh).
bench-run.log

# NOTE: there is deliberately no `results/` pattern here. It used to exist for
# the flat test/performance/results/ directory, and it also matched
# profiles/<name>/results/ — which is the measured data of record, and which
# must be committed. The flat directory is gone; the profiles are tracked.
